!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/a-record-in-place-stating-discriminators-without-abstract-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §5.2 (discriminators beside ABSTRACT, proposed for Revision 40), [TSON-SCHEMA] §5.10.1 (a record written in place, proposed for Revision 40)"
  description: """
    The pair is held in place as at a declaration: a `!meta.record` written at a field's type that states
    `discriminators` and no `extension` is OPEN by the field's default, which is not ABSTRACT, so the schema is a
    resolver error. The sugar `{ kind: text =?  x: int32 }` is the record that loads, lowering to `extension:
    ABSTRACT` beside `discriminators: [kind]`.
    """
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
